-- title:
--   Covered finite-tape chain steps are dominated by the ideal chain
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, let $o_1,o_2$ be Boolean subset-query functions on $[n]$, let $T\in\mathbb N$ be the bounded-draw trial cap, and fix rational $q$ and defect multipliers $w(a)$ indexed by ordered distinct empty/full pair indices. Paired states are subsets of $[n]\times\{0,1\}$. A state is valid when it has one label in every pair, or one empty pair and one full pair with all other pairs single. Assume $q>0$ and $w(a)>0$ for every defect index. Let $\pi$ be the normalized operational weight distribution: the weight is the program's rational weight on a valid state and zero on an invalid state. For states $x,z,y$ and $\alpha\in[0,1]$, put $$E(x,z,y;\alpha)=\alpha\mathbf1_{z=y}+(1-\alpha)\mathbf1_{x=y}.$$ For a Boolean list $h$ and $t\in\mathbb N$, let $\mu_{h,t}$ be the law of a tape obtained by appending $t$ independent fair bits to $h$ and padding with false bits thereafter. A successful run starting at $|h|$ is covered when its final tape position is at most $|h|+t$. Assume additionally $n>0$, and let $x,y$ be paired states with $|x|=n$ and $x$ valid. Let $P$ be the lazy exchange Metropolis chain for $\pi$: it holds with probability one half and otherwise proposes a uniformly selected present/absent exchange and accepts with probability $\min\{1,\pi(z)/\pi(x)\}$. Then $$\mu_{h,t}\{\omega:\exists u\le |h|+t,\ \operatorname{chainStep}_{\omega}(x,|h|)=\operatorname{some}(y,u)\}\le P(x,y).$$
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/CoveredChainStepSubkernel.lean#L188-L271

